Rewrite the L-4 resume check:

```gdscript
var before_files := _log_files(dir)
var before_newest := dir + String(before_files[before_files.size() - 1])
var newest_before := _read_text(before_newest)
var resumed := LogScript.new()
... configure, set_utc_override, record ...
var after_files := _log_files(dir)
# (a) every file retained from before the resume keeps its old bytes as a prefix (append-only, never overwrite)
var newest_now := _read_text(dir + String(after_files[after_files.size() - 1]))
```

However, the retained files after prune may not include the previous latest file. So a generic check: for each file in before_files that still exists in after_files, its current content must begin_with the content read before resume. Need a snapshot map of name→text from before resume.

Implementation in test style:

```gdscript
var before := _snapshot_lines(dir)  # Dictionary name -> text
...
var after := _snapshot_lines(dir)
for name in before:
    if after.has(name) and not String(after[name]).begins_with(String(before[name])):
        return _fail("L4 restart never overwrites existing bytes: " + name)
var newest_now := _read_text(dir + String(after_files[after_files.size() - 1]))
var tail_rows := _split_lines(newest_now)
var tail: Dictionary = JSON.parse_string(tail_rows[tail_rows.size() - 1])
if not _check(String(tail["event"]) == "sale_committed", "L4 appended row is last in newest file")
```

Also add a check that after resume, all files are ≤ 512 (the rotation invariant continues to hold).

